<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!-- The mimic beacon under Combat Extended.

     The same shape as AG_Frost_CE.xml and for the same reasons, which are written out there: CE
     turns every hand grenade into one-use ammo, this one stays reusable so the item is the same
     with or without that mod, and the verb and projectile are deliberately left alone because
     RimArt.Verb_ThrowMimicBeacon defers the launch to MapComponent_Throws for the throw
     animation while CE's verb casts what it spawns straight to ProjectileCE.

     One thing is different here and worth saying. The frost bomb gives up CE's ballistic flight
     for a cell-targeted stun, which is a small loss. The beacon gives up nothing at all: it is a
     device that arrives at a cell and switches on. There is no damage to model, so there is no
     ballistics to miss.

     What CE does change, and should, is the decoy's life expectancy. CE rounds do more damage
     per hit than vanilla's, so a 120-hit-point projection comes apart faster - which is the
     correct direction. The beacon is a way to spend somebody else's ammunition, and CE is a mod
     about ammunition being finite. -->

<Patch>

  <!-- Priced against the frost bomb's 1.1 and CE's own frag grenade at 0.87. The beacon is a
       drum with optics in it rather than a tube of gas: heavier to carry and much more awkward,
       which is the whole of what Bulk says. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AG_MimicBeacon"]/statBases</xpath>
    <value>
      <Bulk>1.4</Bulk>
      <SightsEfficiency>1.0</SightsEfficiency>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Every weapon in CE needs a ToolCE rather than a vanilla Tool, or a pawn who bashes
       somebody with it goes through a code path that expects CE's armour penetration fields and
       does not find them. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AG_MimicBeacon"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <tools>
        <li Class="CombatExtended.ToolCE">
          <label>casing</label>
          <capacities>
            <li>Blunt</li>
          </capacities>
          <power>3</power>
          <cooldownTime>1.9</cooldownTime>
          <armorPenetrationBlunt>1.2</armorPenetrationBlunt>
          <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Base</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        </li>
      </tools>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- One-handed so it can be carried alongside a shield, which is the combination this item is
       for: the pawn throwing the decoy is usually the one covering the retreat. The CE_AI_* tags
       are pointedly absent - they are what tells CE's raider generator to hand a weapon out, and
       nothing in this mod is given to raiders. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AG_MimicBeacon"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <weaponTags>
        <li>CE_OneHandedWeapon</li>
      </weaponTags>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
